{
  "content": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Now that we've explored Hughes and \"Harlem,\" it's time to apply that same process to a poem of your choice!"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": ""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "To do so, choose one (1) poem from the international poetry collection below. Then, explore how the poet uses sound, language, and structure to communicate something about their experiences, identity, or community.",
          "bold": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": ""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Each poem's page will have contextual information about the poet and a recording of the poem. "
        },
        {
          "text": "Regardless of the poem you choose, you will:",
          "bold": true,
          "underline": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "numbered-list",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "list-item",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Listen to a reading of your chosen poem and annotate as you listen"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list-item",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Add to your annotations, following the annotation procedure modeled with Hughes's \"Harlem.\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list-item",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Synthesize your ideas together into a 3-5 minute oral analysis, answering the following prompt: \"How do individuals navigate their relationships with the communities around them? Use textual evidence and poetic devices to discuss how your poem explores this question, being sure to address how your poet utilizes sound to do so.\""
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Your instructor will give more specific instructions for how they would like for you to annotate, record, and submit your materials, so be sure to follow their guidance."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": ""
        }
      ]
